<p>A core in any other language is an implementation when it follows the specification and passes <code>acid-cat conform</code>.</p>
<ol>
  <li>Follow the <a href="/spec/">specification</a>.</li>
  <li>Serve the <a href="/spec/conformance/#the-conformance-fixture">conformance fixture</a>, <code>packages/cli/conformance/fixture.pkl</code>, through each binding of your core.</li>
  <li>Test each binding from outside with <code>acid-cat conform</code>:</li>
</ol>
<Code code={ownCore.conform} lang="sh" />
<p><a href="/docs/guides/test-with-conform/">Test an implementation with acid-cat conform</a> gives every flag.</p>
